The main interpretation is still open. The saved H1 summary characterises evidence as modest and notes a fixed-sample sensitivity check. H2 does not detect an age difference in tone change. H2b emerged during exploration and varies in significance across controls and instruments. The datasets have different eligibility rules and periods, and Guardian coverage concerns one publication. These features constrain how recruitment and reception can be discussed together.

